    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0019" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation 3/130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-29T13:00:00-04:00">December 29, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>837. For the Under Secretary. Rossetti asks me to request that you see him before
                    opening session. Am warning him subtly as possible about commitments en route.
                    Mexican Ambassador showed me cable from his Government expressing concern over
                    fact most Foreign Ministers will have 3 or 4 days with element that was not
                    helpful at Lima<anchor n="9" xml:id="d6-f1"/> and Habana.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d6-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
